{
  "requirement": "A GitHub Actions CI workflow MUST run, for pull requests and pushes to `main`, these checks: `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace` under {cite}`requirements.test-coverage.run`, `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`, `mdbook test`, the autofix controller tests with `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`, and, in a separate job, the Symposium session-start hook smoke test `tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`. It also builds the book as documentation under {cite}`requirements.index.render_only`, without requiring collected execution reports for rendering. On a push to `main`, only after every check job passes, it deploys the generated `book/` directory to GitHub Pages. The book MUST set `output.html.site-url` to `/habeas-codicem/` for project-site hosting.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The single marked test, `tests/repository.rs#fn[ci_tests_pull_requests_and_main_then_deploys_the_book_from_main]`, covers each obligation in `requirements.integration.ci`. I read `.github/workflows/ci.yml` to check that the asserted strings match the real workflow.\n\n- **Triggers:** the test asserts the exact `on:` block, with `push` on `branches: [main]` and `pull_request`.\n- **Required checks:** in the `test-and-build` job it asserts the presence and order of these steps:\n  - `node --test .github/scripts/autofix.test.mjs`\n  - the habeas build\n  - `cargo habeas coverage -- --locked --workspace`\n  - `cargo habeas coverage-check`\n  - `cargo test --locked --doc --workspace`\n  - `mdbook test`\n  - `mdbook build`\n  - the pages artifact upload with `path: book`\n  \n  It also asserts, from the parsed YAML, that the coverage-check gate has no `if` and no `continue-on-error`.\n- **Separate hook job:** it asserts that a separate `symposium-hook` job runs `python3 tests/symposium_hook_smoke.py`.\n- **Deploy:** it asserts that the `deploy` job has `if: github.event_name == 'push' && github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'`. It asserts `needs: [test-and-build, symposium-hook]`, so deploy waits for every check job. It also asserts `actions/deploy-pages@v4`.\n- **Book as documentation:** the `mdbook build` step is asserted to run after coverage collection and before the artifact upload. The cited `requirements.index.render_only` behavior, rendering without execution reports, belongs to that requirement's own tests and is not reassessed here. `requirements.test-coverage.run` is likewise cited context only.\n- **`site-url`:** it asserts that `site-url` equals `/habeas-codicem/`. The key it reads is `output.habeas.html.site-url`, because the book uses the habeas renderer wrapper. The requirement text says `output.html.site-url`. `book.toml` has no `[output.html]` table. I treated this as a looseness in the requirement's wording, not a test-adequacy gap.\n\nI found no obligation that is untested or asserted wrongly.",
